  "rationale": "The pivot child becomes the new root, while its inner subtree moves between the old and new roots. A rotation is a local topology change, not a search or a whole-tree mirror.",
  "commonMistakes": [
    "return-original-topology",
    "discard-pivot-inner-subtree",
    "rotate-in-the-opposite-direction"
  ],
